Step-by-step execution
Step 1 — Create the experiment files
Inside your Generative-AI-Laboratory GitHub repository, create:
- Experiment-05-MNIST-GAN/README.md
- Experiment-05-MNIST-GAN/gan.py
- Experiment-05-MNIST-GAN/requirements.txt
- Experiment-05-MNIST-GAN/output.txt
- Experiment-05-MNIST-GAN/.gitignore
Step 2 — Set up Python locally
Open the experiment folder in VS Code.

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Activate it in Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Step 3 — Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 4 — Execute the GAN

python gan.py



The program downloads MNIST on the first run if it is not cached, trains the Generator and Discriminator for 20 epochs, and saves generated images and training graphs.

Training can be time-consuming on a CPU. For a quick initial check, temporarily set EPOCHS = 1 in gan.py. Restore EPOCHS = 20 for the full experiment.
Step 5 — Verify results
Open the outputs/ directory and check the generated digit grids and loss graph.

If the images remain noisy, possible improvements include longer training, adjusting learning rates, or using a convolutional GAN architecture.
